Description:
    Installs the transactional outbox tables into the host application. The
    Strata event models, router, and jobs are shipped by the
    engine directly — only the migration is copied.

Usage:
    bin/rails generate strata:events

This will create:
    - db/migrate/<timestamp>_create_strata_events.rb

Options:
    --skip-migration-check         Skip checking if the Strata event tables exist

After generating:
    bin/rails db:migrate

About domain events:
    Strata::EventManager.publish keeps its existing name and payload arguments,
    but records a durable Strata::Event in the caller's current database
    transaction. Wrap the domain change and publish call in one explicit
    transaction when they must be atomic. Dispatch happens after commit so a
    rolled-back domain change cannot leave behind an event.

    Register business processes by class name. The generator normally adds this
    configuration automatically:

        config.to_prepare do
          Strata::Events.register "PassportBusinessProcess"
        end

    Each committed event is processed by a Strata dispatch job, which inherits
    the host application's configured Active Job adapter. The job routes the
    event and attempts its handler deliveries sequentially. Hosts can use
    :inline for synchronous in-process work or a durable adapter for
    cross-process delivery.

    Production hosts must configure a durable application adapter and run its
    workers. Strata jobs inherit that adapter automatically. Rails' default
    AsyncAdapter is process-local and does not survive restarts.

        # config/environments/production.rb (example)
        config.active_job.queue_adapter = :solid_queue

    Strata persists delivery failures and retry times instead of using Active
    Job retry scheduling. Run the sweep task repeatedly from cron or another
    scheduler to recover undispatched events and retry due deliveries:

        bin/rails strata:events:sweep

    Configure retention explicitly, then invoke the prune job or rake task
    periodically from a recurring scheduler:

        bin/rails generate strata:audit_log # required for accountable pruning
        bin/rails db:migrate

        Strata::Events.configure do |config|
          config.routing_retry_delay = 5.minutes
          config.retention_days = 90
        end

        Strata::Events::PruneJob.perform_later # performs one pruning run

    One-off recovery and retention tasks:

        bin/rails strata:events:sweep
        bin/rails "strata:events:prune[90]" DRY_RUN=1
        bin/rails "strata:events:prune[90]"
